.\" Generated by odir --write-man-pages from the console grammar; do not edit.
.TH "ODIR-SETBANDWIDTH" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-setbandwidth \- setbandwidth: Sets bandwidth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
setbandwidth [client=<client>] [fd=<fd>] [storage=<storage>] [sd=<sd>] [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [job=<job>] [ujobid=<ujobid>] [state=<state>] [all] [limit=<limit>] [yes]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Limits the bandwidth of a File Daemon, a Storage Daemon or running jobs without changing the configuration. The Director connects to the daemon and sends the new limit in kB/s; it applies until the daemon restarts or the job ends. limit=0 removes the limit; a missing limit is asked for. NDMP storages cannot be limited.
.PP
job=, jobid=, ujobid=, all and state= select running jobs. For backup and restore the limit is applied through the File Daemon, for copy and migrate through the reading Storage Daemon. Without client, storage or a job selection the Director asks for the client.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "setbandwidth"
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "fd=<fd>"
Client name (as client=) (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "sd=<sd>"
Storage name (as storage=) (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job ID (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "ujobid=<ujobid>"
Unique job name (text)
.TP
.B "state=<state>"
Jobs in this state (text)
.TP
.B "all"
Every running job (keyword)
.TP
.B "limit=<limit>"
KiB/s (0: unlimited) (number)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "setbandwidth limit=10000 client=bareos\-fd"
throttle the File Daemon to about 10 MB/s
.TP
.B "setbandwidth limit=5000 jobid=42"
slow down the running job 42
.TP
.B "setbandwidth limit=0 client=bareos\-fd"
remove the limit again
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
